build.summary:
I built proc-hypotension-pressors. Every acceptance criterion passes: 39 tests across the five test files below, and the typecheck is clean for every file in this package.

There is now one shared hypotension-cause model (src/simulation/patient/hypotensionCauses.ts). It has 12 core causes: bleeding, fasting, ischaemia, tamponade, complete heart block, nitrate after a PDE-5 inhibitor, verapamil, vasodilation in obstructive HCM, vagal, contrast reaction, a transducer above the heart, and air in the line. Each cause has:
- its mechanism (hypovolaemia, cardiac failure, vasodilation, or a false reading);
- its signature (filling, RA, output, rate, and whether a cuff agrees with the line);
- the treatment of the cause, and which drugs suit it as a bridge;
- a script that starts it on the engine using only public engine methods.

The model also classifies a right heart readout using Brilakis's pattern, and other labs can add their own causes with registerHypotensionCause.

The full-case driver is two files: src/simulation/session/hypotension.ts (pump list with sourced dose ranges, orders, oedema regimen, pure scoring rules) and the session module src/simulation/session/modules/hypotension.ts. The module:
- runs the scenario's cause and opens a hypotension episode from the pressure the monitor shows;
- offers the 'is it real' checks (cuff, zero, level, flush, look at the trace) through the session's own methods;
- gives right heart numbers: measured through a venous sheath, or a modelled reading with a note when there is none;
- gives volume, blood, cause treatments (control the bleeding site, pericardial drain, pacing, atropine), phenylephrine boluses and eight infusion pumps (drug, syringe strength, dose rate, mL/h, line);
- adds the oedema orders: oxygen, sit up, furosemide 80 or 100 mg, CPAP, and a nitrate pump.

It scores these decisions: was the pressure confirmed real, did the drug suit the mechanism, was the cause treated, was the mechanism named ('empty, failing or dilated'), was dobutamine started low, which line was used, the escalation choice, weaning, the oedema bolus, the nitrate at low pressure, and the oedema first steps.

Several consequences come from the modelled patient rather than fixed rules:
- **Rising doses:** a dose above its range can bring on VT (from the module's own seeded draw), which settles once the dose is back in range.
- **Rebound:** a pressor left running after the cause is fixed raises the pressure.
- **Escalation question:** asked once doses rise; choosing mechanical support hands the patient to the support lab and opens it.
- **Oedema:** a fluid bolus into a raised LVEDP drops the SpO2 through the engine's own oxygenation model.

The ten scenarios and their .launch.ts are in src/simulation/session/scenarios/. The UI is the order section src/ui/access/orders/Infusions.tsx with src/ui/access/InfusionPanel.tsx, built in the Clinical Graphite style with generic names. The live screen never names the cause, and drug ranges are shown only in guided mode.

The cause model has no effect on random cases: one test runs the same seed with and without the module and gets the same patient. The listed files did not exist before, so the snapshot folder holds only .started.
